.TH MAD 1 "2026-11-24" "mad-terminal 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mad \- the MAD Terminal: grade before you sign
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mad
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mad
is the terminal for MAD, the angry auditor of the agent economy
(Mad Check, https://madcheck.xyz). It grades claims against receipts
before you sign or pay: agent registrations, payment authorizations,
x402 endpoints, and token launches. Every verdict comes with the
evidence it was derived from. Nobody is paid to pass, and the graded
never pays.
.PP
MAD talks back. Every output is in the auditor's voice \- blunt, angry,
sarcastic \- and every screen wears MAD's face, drawn from MAD's own
avatar (@MADx402). The face is the flaming auditor; never a human face.
.PP
Free doors first, always. The paid doors cost 0.01 USDC via x402 on
Base. This terminal NEVER pays: on a 402 it prints the bill and exits
3. Re-run with
.B --payment
and a payload you signed elsewhere if you want the verdict.
.PP
The terminal is alive: bare
.B mad
wakes MAD up with what moved since your last run (witness seq, dust,
freshest grade) and the next check worth your time. State lives in
.I ~/.cache/mad-terminal/state.json
\\- delete it any time and MAD starts over with no memory. Every
verdict travels three lanes to the same answer: the API door live, a
pre-computed lane (the grades feed, or MAD's own memory of your last
checks), and the chained witness ledger, head links recomputed here.
A lane that can't be reached says so; it never fakes agreement.
.B mad fix
is the fix back: a FAIL prints the fix, and the safe, reversible ones
are applied only when you say yes. Nothing here signs or moves money,
ever.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B mad
With no arguments, drops into the interactive REPL: type plain English
and MAD answers back, routing to the right command.
.TP
.B mad talk
Same REPL, on purpose.
.TP
.B mad test [--agent-id N] [--chain base|robinhood] [--url URL]
THE MAD TEST: the free five-station battery. Grades yourself by
default (MAD's own id, 1224530).
.TP
.B mad check agent <id> [--chain base|robinhood]
Grade an ERC-8004 registration: LIVE / DEAD END / GHOST / MALFORMED.
0.01 USDC.
.TP
.B mad check authorization --from 0x.. --to 0x.. --value N --valid-after S --valid-before S --nonce 0x.. --chain-id 8453 --verifying-contract 0x..
The signing firewall: SIGN / DONT_SIGN, with reasons. 0.01 USDC.
.TP
.B mad check endpoint <url>
Is the door alive, and what does it answer. 0.01 USDC.
.TP
.B mad seal <address>
Born Graded seal lookup: SEALED / UNSEALED / FAILED. Free. The
contract address, never the name or ticker.
.TP
.B mad witness [seq]
The signed witness ledger: head, or one entry by sequence number. Free.
.TP
.B mad dust pool
The MAD DUST pool: backing, liability, reserve. Free.
.TP
.B mad dust ledger [--offset N] [--limit N]
The public hash-chained dust ledger. Free.
.TP
.B mad dust balance <chainId> <agentId>
One identity's dust. Free.
.TP
.B mad feed [--limit N]
The grades feed, newest first. Free.
.TP
.B mad complain file --claimant-name X --respondent-name Y --claim "..." [--category payable|broken_promise|number_mismatch|other]
File a complaint on the Complaint Desk. Free, public to both parties
the moment it lands, UNGRADED until MAD grades it.
.TP
.B mad complain list
Every filing on the desk. Free.
.TP
.B mad complain get CMP-0001
One filing in full. Free.
.TP
.B mad ask "<plain English>"
Say it like a human; MAD routes it deterministically (no LLM).
"grade this agent 1224530", "is 0x... sealed", "show the witness head".
.TP
.B mad mcp [--ping]
The MCP server config block for Claude, Codex, and Grok
(https://api.madcheck.xyz/mcp, 7 tools). --ping checks the door live.
.TP
.B mad fix [agent <id> | seal <address> | endpoint <url> | authorization ...]
Re-grade the target live, print the fix for every failing finding,
and apply the safe, reversible ones only when you say yes: a
corrected authorization file (same value, same recipient, 5-minute
window), a claim-sheet draft for an UNSEALED token, a direct re-probe
of a dead door. Bare
.B mad fix
fixes the last thing MAD graded in this terminal.
.TP
.B mad version
Version and identity.
.TP
.B mad help
This text, with the face at the foot of it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help, -h
This help, anywhere on the line: `mad test --help` works.
.TP
.B --version, -v
Version and identity, anywhere on the line: `mad check --version`.
.TP
.B --json
Machine mode: raw JSON on stdout (MAD still talks, on stderr). The
402 bill is a JSON object in this mode.
.TP
.B --payment <base64>
Resend with a signed x402 payload you made elsewhere. mad never signs.
.TP
.B --chain base|robinhood
Chain for the call. Base 8453 is the default; Robinhood Chain is 4663.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The call landed and the verdict is in the output.
.TP
.B 1
The API answered and it wasn't good news.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: a missing id, a bad address, a flag MAD doesn't know.
.TP
.B 3
Payment required: the door printed its 402 bill. Pay it, then come back.
.TP
.B 4
Transport failure: the line died. Never a verdict.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAD_API
API base URL. Default https://api.madcheck.xyz.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set to disable colour (plain ASCII face, plain text).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mad test
mad check agent 1224530
mad seal 0x1bc0c42215582d5A085795f4baDbaC3ff36d1Bcb
mad witness
mad mcp --ping
mad ask "grade this agent 1224530"
mad fix seal 0x1bc0c42215582d5A085795f4baDbaC3ff36d1Bcb
.fi
